{title: 465 - I Heard the Voice of Jesus}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #465 • KINGSFOLD • C.M.D.}
{lyricist: Horatius Bonar}
{composer: Lucy Broadwood}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 465}
{meta: tune KINGSFOLD}
{meta: meter C.M.D.}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]I heard [C/G]the voice of [D/F#]Jesus [G]say,
[C/G]“Come unto [Bm/D]Me [C]and rest;
[C/G]Lay [G]down, thou weary [Em/B]one, lay down
[D/F#]Thy head [G]upon My [D7/C]breast.”
[D7/F#]Icame [G]to Jesus [Em]as I was,
[G]Weary [Bm]and worn [D7/C]and sad;
[Em/B]I [D]found in [G]Him a [D7/C]resting [Em/B]place,
[Em/G]And He has made [G]me glad.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am]I heard [C/G]the voice of [D/F#]Jesus [G]say,
[C/G]"Behold, [Bm]I freely [C]give
[C/G]The [G]living water; [Em/B]thirsty one,
[D/F#]Stoop down [G]and drink and [D7/C]live."
[D7/F#]I came [G]to Jesus, [Em]and I drank
[G]Of that [Bm]life giving [D7/C]stream;
[Em/B]My [D]thirst was [G]quench'd, my [D7/C]soul revived,
[Em/G]And now I live [G]in Him.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am]I heard [C/G]the voice of [D/F#]Jesus [G]say,
[C/G]"I am [Bm]this dark [C]world's light;
[C/G]Look [G]unto Me, [C/G]thy [Em/B]morn shall rise,
[D/F#]And all [G]thy day be [D7/C]bright."
[D7/F#]I looked [G]to Jesus, [Em]and I found
[G]In Him [Bm]my star, [D7/C]my sun;
[Em/B]And [D]in that [G]light of [D7/C]life I'll [Em/B]walk,
[Em/G]Till trav'ling days [G]are done.
{end_of_verse}
